      "name": "InitializeGlobalDataStructures",
      "signature": "void InitializeGlobalDataStructures(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize global data structures and arrays for application startup.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Set up structured exception handling with SEH frame and canary guard\\n2. Allocate 0x14-byte control structure (doubly-linked list node)\\n3. Initialize list node pointers (prev, next, self) and flags\\n4. Load initialization data from 36 global data regions\\n5. For each data region, call FUN_0427c870 to construct vector/array\\n6. Register main data structure with FUN_0427c910 callback\\n7. Register exception vector destructor for cleanup\\n8. Restore exception handler and verify stack canary\\n\\nReturns: void (no return value)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Global data regions start at 0x0433ffe0 and continue through 0x043401d0\\n- All array initializations use the FUN_0427c870 vector constructor\\n- Exception handling uses __stdcall convention with SEH frame\\n- Stack guard canary XORed with frame pointer for corruption detection\\n- 0x14-byte structure initialized with self-referential list pointers and marker value 0x101\\n- Exit handler registered via _atexit for proper cleanup\\n- Destructor iterator processes 0x26 elements of 8 bytes each",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
