      "name": "InitializeGameDataTables",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameDataTables(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes all game data tables and structures during startup sequence\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate and initialize linked list head structure (14 bytes with self-references)\n2. Initialize state counter to 0 for exception handling tracking\n3. Create 36 game data tables in sequence:\n   - Tables 0-5: Index sequences (2-7, various target values)\n   - Tables 6-8: Loaded from global data regions (DWORD arrays)\n   - Tables 9-15: Additional index sequences with magic values\n   - Tables 16-23: Complex multi-DWORD entries from global data\n   - Tables 24-35: Final sequence entries and computed indices\n4. Call FUN_0427c910 to register main data handler with all table heads\n5. Register vector destructor for cleanup via eh_vector_destructor_iterator\n6. Register atexit handler at DAT_04325a70 for shutdown cleanup\n7. Perform stack guard verification and restore exception list\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses global game data structures\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies global state, no return value\n\nStructure Layout:\nData table head structure (14 bytes):\nOffset 0x00: self_reference (DWORD) = data table head address\nOffset 0x04: next_list_head (DWORD) = data table head address\nOffset 0x08: prev_list_head (DWORD) = data table head address\nOffset 0x0C: table_count (WORD) = 0x0101 (257 entries marker)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:da19008991f295eb8f0c860718c23696",
