      "name": "InitializeScreenFunction",
      "signature": "void InitializeScreenFunction(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the global screen function pointer by retrieving it from the game's function table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetD2FunctionPointer() helper to retrieve the screen function pointer reference\n2. Dereference the pointer to obtain the actual function pointer value\n3. Store the function pointer in global variable gScreenFunction (0x0435b3a4) for later use\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The function pointer is ordinal 0xc in the D2 function table\n- The global variable gScreenFunction is initialized on first call\n- Actual function retrieval is delegated to GetD2FunctionPointer() which handles version detection",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
