      "name": "CacheD2FunctionPointer",
      "signature": "void CacheD2FunctionPointer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Caches a Diablo II function pointer to global storage.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls GetD2FunctionPointerRef to obtain a cached pointer to a D2 function\n2. Dereferences the returned pointer to extract the actual D2 function address\n3. Stores the extracted function address in global cache DAT_0435b3a0\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function stores result in global variable, no return value\n\nPurpose:\n  This function is part of the D2 function wrapper system. It retrieves a cached\n  D2 function pointer from lazy-initialized storage and makes it available through\n  a global variable for other code to invoke.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - First call to GetD2FunctionPointerRef triggers full initialization including\n    game version detection and D2 library function discovery\n  - Subsequent calls use cached value without re-initialization\n  - Global storage location (0x0435b3a0) may be shared with other wrapper functions",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
