      "name": "InitializeGameFunctionPointer",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameFunctionPointer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes and caches a D2 game function pointer from GetD2FunctionPointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_04274a60() to get pointer to cached function pointer variable\n2. Dereference the returned pointer to extract the actual function pointer value\n3. Store the function pointer at global address 0x0435b3e4 for later use\n\nReturns: void (result stored in global cache at 0x0435b3e4)\n\nPurpose: This function is used to retrieve and cache Diablo II function pointers\nduring game initialization. The cached pointer at 0x0435b3e4 is accessed by multiple\ncalling functions that need the D2 function reference.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- FUN_04274a60() handles version detection and caching internally\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention with no parameters\n- Global destination address 0x0435b3e4 is a D2 function pointer storage location",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
