      "name": "GetGlobalInitializationValue",
      "signature": "void GetGlobalInitializationValue(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves initialization value from function pointer and stores to global.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls FUN_04275ba0 to obtain a function pointer\n2. Dereferences the returned pointer to get the actual value\n3. Stores the dereferenced value to global variable at 0x0435b3e0\n4. Returns void\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; result stored in global memory\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis is a simple wrapper/initialization function that acts as an indirection\nlayer for retrieving and caching a computed initialization value. The function\npointer returned by FUN_04275ba0 is dereferenced to obtain the actual data,\nwhich suggests the callee returns a reference to a static or dynamically\ncomputed value.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
