      "name": "CacheDynamicFunctionPointer",
      "signature": "void CacheDynamicFunctionPointer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Wrapper function that caches a dynamically resolved function pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_04275c60() which performs lazy initialization of a cached function pointer\n2. Dereference the returned pointer to get the actual cached function value\n3. Store the cached function pointer to the global variable DAT_0435b3d8\n4. Return to caller\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nPurpose:\n  This is a thunk/wrapper that ensures DAT_0435b3dc is initialized with the\n  resolved function pointer before returning. The actual initialization logic\n  is in FUN_04275c60, which handles version detection and D2 function resolution.\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\n  DAT_0435b3d8 - Receives the cached function pointer value\n\nRelated Functions:\n  FUN_04275c60 - Performs lazy initialization and returns cached pointer address\n  GetD2FunctionPointer - Used by FUN_04275c60 to resolve D2 functions by ordinal",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
