      "name": "InitializeGlobalObjects",
      "signature": "void InitializeGlobalObjects(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize global C++ objects and data structures for the application.\n\nThis function is a global static construction function that initializes multiple C++ objects\nat program startup. It creates a doubly-linked list structure, allocates and initializes\n36 distinct data objects with varying sizes and field values, registers cleanup handlers,\nand sets up exception handling for controlled termination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up SEH exception handler chain with FS:[0] and stack guard canary\n2. Initialize uStack_8 error state counter (starts at 0xffffffff)\n3. Allocate 20-byte linked list node via operator_new()\n4. Initialize list node fields: prev/next pointers (self-referential), spare field 0x101\n5. Iterate 36 times (phases 0-35), each phase:\n   a. Increment uStack_8 phase counter (_0_1_ byte access)\n   b. Load 3 parameters (typically integer constants and data references)\n   c. Call FUN_0427c870() to construct object with parameters\n   d. Store constructed object in local stack array variable\n6. After all phases complete, call FUN_0427c910() with DAT_0435b3b4 (global registry)\n7. Register FUN_04325a90() cleanup function via _atexit()\n8. Clean up exception handler, verify stack guard, and return\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function - called as static constructor)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Function performs initialization side effects.\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic values: 0x101 in list node offset +0xc (reserved field), 0xffffffff initial error state\nError handling: Uses SEH with exception handler at LAB_0431a7b2, FS:[0] chain\nStack layout: 0x318 bytes local storage (784 bytes) for 36+ object instances\nPhase progression: uStack_8._0_1_ incremented 0x00 through 0x25 (38 distinct phases)\nRegister protection: StackGuardCanary XOR'd with EBP and stack address for overflow detection\nCleanup registration: _atexit(FUN_04325a90) ensures proper destruction order\nException safety: eh_vector_destructor_iterator called with 0x26 size, 0x8 element stride\n\nStructure Layout (List Node):\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n  0x0    4    prev_ptr          void*     Points to previous node (self-referential initially)\n  0x4    4    next_ptr          void*     Points to next node (self-referential initially)\n  0x8    4    data_ptr          void*     Points to data or self\n  0xC    2    reserved_field    uint16    Fixed value 0x101\n  0xE    2    (padding)         -         Unused padding\nTotal structure size: 0x10 (16 bytes minimum), actual allocation 0x14 (20 bytes)",
