      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleanup and deallocate global resource structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the global resource pointer from DAT_0435b6d0\n2. Retrieve the cleanup handler pointer from offset +4 of the resource structure\n3. Call the resource cleanup function with the resource pointer and handler pointer\n4. Free the global resource memory\n5. Return to caller\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Returns without value after cleanup complete\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assumes DAT_0435b6d0 contains a pointer to a resource structure\n- The structure at DAT_0435b6d0 + 0x4 contains a function pointer for cleanup\n- No validation of pointer validity is performed\n- This function is called as part of application shutdown",
