      "comment": "Cleanup and free a global data structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the global data structure from address 0x0435b6f0\n2. Load nested pointer from offset +4 within the structure\n3. Call FUN_04282f50 to process/clean both the base structure and nested pointer\n4. Prepare memory deallocation parameters (size = 0x2c / 44 bytes)\n5. Call memory deallocator function to free the structure\n6. Return to caller\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Access:\n  Offset 0x0: Base pointer to global structure\n  Offset 0x4: Pointer to nested structure data within base\n\nNotes:\n  Cleanup/finalization function for global data structures.\n  The 44-byte size matches typical Diablo II game data allocations.\n  Called from data initialization shutdown sequences.",
