      "name": "ClearContainerItems",
      "signature": "void ClearContainerItems(int * pContainer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Clears all items from a dynamic container and releases memory.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load container address (0x435b6ac) into ECX\\n2. Pass container pointer to cleanup function via __fastcall\\n3. Cleanup function iterates through all items (stride 0xC bytes)\\n4. Calls destructor on each item via FUN_04279a10\\n5. Validates memory integrity before freeing\\n6. Deallocates container memory and zeroes pointers\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pContainer (ECX via __fastcall): Pointer to container structure with:\\n  - [0] = begin pointer (first item address)\\n  - [1] = end pointer (past-last item address)\\n  - [2] = capacity (end of allocated memory)\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - Container is modified in-place\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Item size: 0xC (12 bytes), calculated from (end - begin) / 0xC\\n- Empty container: No cleanup if begin pointer is null\\n- Corruption detection: Validates memory block header before freeing\\n- Item iteration: Walks from begin to end pointer in 0xC byte strides\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\n| Offset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description |\\n|--------|------|-----------|------|-------------|\\n| 0x00   | 4    | begin     | void* | Pointer to first item |\\n| 0x04   | 4    | end       | void* | Pointer to past-last item |\\n| 0x08   | 4    | capacity  | void* | Pointer to end of allocation |",
