      "name": "InitializeGameState",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the game state by loading the global game context and delegating to the core initialization routine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load ECX with the address of the global game state structure (0x435b678)\n2. Jump to the real initialization function (FUN_0427dee0) with context loaded\n3. The target function performs actual state initialization with the context\n\nParameters:\nNone - This is a wrapper that loads the implicit context parameter\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No value returned. The function performs side effects on global state.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This function serves as an entry point that bridges the call site and the real initialization logic\n- The global game state at 0x435b678 must be allocated and valid before this call\n- Uses an implicit context passing pattern where ECX contains the state pointer\n- This is a __stdcall function with no stack parameters\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe game state structure at 0x435b678 is passed to FUN_0427dee0 for initialization. The exact layout depends on the target function's implementation.",
