      "name": "FreeGlobalBuffer",
      "signature": "void FreeGlobalBuffer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Deallocates and validates a globally managed memory buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global buffer pointer (DAT_0435b66c) is non-null; exit if null\n2. Calculate allocated size: (end_ptr - buffer_ptr) & 0xfffffffc, mask to 4-byte alignment\n3. Validate allocation size >= 0x1000 bytes\n4. Read allocation header pointer from offset -4 before buffer start\n5. Calculate actual allocation size: (buffer_ptr - 4) - header_ptr\n6. Validate allocation metadata is within bounds (<= 0x1f bytes)\n7. Call FreeMemory() with calculated allocation header and size\n8. Reset three global state variables to zero\n9. Jump to CorruptionDetected() if validation fails at step 6\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Function operates entirely on global state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Either deallocates successfully or triggers CorruptionDetected()\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x1000: Minimum allocation size threshold for validation\n- Magic number 0x1f (31 bytes): Maximum allowed allocation metadata overhead\n- Magic number 0xfffffffc: 4-byte alignment mask for size calculation\n- Allocation header stored at offset -4 from buffer pointer\n- Function never returns on corruption; calls non-returning CorruptionDetected()\n\nGlobal State:\nDAT_0435b66c - Buffer pointer (cleared to 0)\nDAT_0435b670 - State variable (cleared to 0)\nDAT_0435b674 - Buffer end pointer (cleared to 0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
