      "name": "FreeAndClearGlobalBuffer",
      "signature": "void FreeAndClearGlobalBuffer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Frees and clears a globally-managed buffer with integrity validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global buffer pointer from DAT_0435b6d8\n2. If pointer is null, skip to cleanup (optimization for repeated calls)\n3. Load allocation size from DAT_0435b6e0 (size tracking global)\n4. Calculate allocated size: (DAT_0435b6e0 - buffer_ptr) & 0xfffffffc\n5. Validate allocation size is greater than 0x1000 (4KB minimum), else jump to free\n6. Load allocation header metadata from buffer_ptr[-4] (contains original allocation base)\n7. Add magic constant 0x23 to calculated size for verification\n8. Calculate metadata offset: buffer_ptr - header_base - 4\n9. Validate metadata offset is not greater than 0x1f (31 bytes), triggers corruption detection\n10. Call FreeMemory(header_base) with allocation size parameter to deallocate\n11. Clear DAT_0435b6d8 (buffer pointer), DAT_0435b6dc (flags), DAT_0435b6e0 (size)\n12. Return normally\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Modifies global state by clearing DAT_0435b6d8, DAT_0435b6dc, DAT_0435b6e0.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_0435b6d8 is null, function returns immediately (safe for repeated calls)\n- If allocation size check fails (less than 0x1000), jumps directly to FreeMemory call\n- If metadata validation fails (offset > 0x1f), calls CorruptionDetected() and never returns\n- Magic constant 0x23 added during size calculation suggests protocol/alignment padding\n- Metadata stored at offset -4 from returned pointer indicates allocation wrapper pattern\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- DAT_0435b6d8: Buffer pointer (cleared to 0 after free)\n- DAT_0435b6dc: Associated flags/state (cleared to 0)\n- DAT_0435b6e0: Allocation size tracking (cleared to 0)",
