      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleanup handler executed at program exit. Performs graceful shutdown of game resources and interfaces.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call primary cleanup routine for game data structures\n2. Check if game state/context pointer is initialized (non-null)\n3. If initialized, call virtual method at offset +8 (typically Query Interface)\n4. Check if interface returned successfully\n5. If interface valid, call virtual method at offset 0 with parameter 1\n6. Return to caller (atexit handler cleanup complete)\n\nParameters:\nNone - This is an atexit handler registered with no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; called automatically at program termination\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles null pointer checks at two levels (game state and interface pointer)\n- Uses virtual method dispatch pattern (vtable at offset 0 and 8)\n- Parameter value 1 suggests cleanup/shutdown flag or mode selection\n- Called during normal program exit sequence via atexit() registration",
