      "name": "ResetMemoryPool",
      "signature": "void ResetMemoryPool(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Resets the memory pool to initial state and validates integrity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if current pool size (DAT_043559d0) exceeds threshold 0xf\n2. Load pool buffer pointer from DAT_043559bc\n3. Validate that incremented size does not exceed 0x1000 (4096)\n4. Retrieve size field from memory location [buffer - 4]\n5. Calculate allocation overhead by subtracting header size (-4) from buffer offset\n6. If overhead exceeds 0x1f (31 bytes), call CorruptionDetected() and halt\n7. If validation passes, call FreeMemory() with the buffer pointer\n8. Reset pool state: set DAT_043559cc to 0, DAT_043559d0 to 0xf\n9. Align pool buffer address to 256-byte boundary (AND with 0xffffff00)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic numbers: 0xf (15) is minimum pool size threshold\n- 0x1000 (4096) is maximum pool size limit\n- 0x1f (31) is maximum allowed allocation overhead\n- 0xffffff00 aligns buffer to 256-byte boundaries\n- CorruptionDetected() is a non-returning function (halt)\n- Pool pointer is stored at DAT_043559bc with size at DAT_043559d0\n- Allocation headers are stored 4 bytes before the buffer pointer\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type     | Description\n-------|------|---------------|----------|---------------------------------------------\n0xbc   | 4    | PoolBuffer    | LPVOID   | Pointer to memory pool buffer\n0xcc   | 4    | PoolState     | DWORD    | Pool state flags (0 when valid)\n0xd0   | 4    | PoolSize      | DWORD    | Current pool size (0xf minimum)",
