      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Deallocates a tracked memory buffer and resets buffer tracking globals.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check if global buffer pointer (DAT_0435b780) is non-null; exit if null\\n2. Calculate remaining buffer size by subtracting buffer start from buffer end (DAT_0435b788)\\n3. Align size downward to 4-byte boundary using AND with 0xfffffffc\\n4. Verify size does not exceed maximum threshold of 0x1000 bytes\\n5. Read memory allocation header from offset -4 before buffer start\\n6. Calculate header offset distance from buffer pointer to allocation base\\n7. Validate header offset does not exceed 0x1f bytes (corruption check)\\n8. Call FreeMemory() to deallocate the entire memory block from header\\n9. Clear all three buffer tracking globals to null (0x0435b780, 0x0435b784, 0x0435b788)\\n10. Return to caller\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- If buffer pointer is null (0x0), function returns immediately without action\\n- If allocated buffer exceeds 0x1000 bytes, memory is still deallocated\\n- If header offset exceeds 0x1f bytes, calls CorruptionDetected() which does not return\\n- The -4 byte header stores the allocation header address for freeing entire block\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nMemory layout includes 4-byte allocation header followed by allocated buffer:\\nOffset | Size | Field Name     | Type    | Description\\n0      | 4    | alloc_header   | LPVOID  | Allocation base pointer (stored at offset -4 from buffer)\\n4      | N    | buffer_data    | byte[]  | Actual allocated buffer data",
