      "comment": "Destroys the Amazon skills array by calling the destructor for each element.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Invoke the vector destructor iterator function to safely destroy all skill elements\n2. Iterate through 7 skill elements, each 0x1c bytes in size\n3. Call the destructor function (FUN_0428b9a0) for each element to clean up allocated memory\n4. Return after all destructors complete\n\nParameters:\n  None - operates on static data structure\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Destructs exactly 7 elements from the Amazon skills array\n  - Element size is fixed at 0x1c (28) bytes\n  - Each element represents a skill configuration with potential dynamically allocated memory\n  - The destructor function handles freeing internal allocations and validation\n\nStructure Layout:\n  The array at 0x04357278 contains 7 elements, each 28 bytes:\n  Offset    Size    Field Name         Type        Description\n  0x00      4       unknown0           uint        Unused/padding\n  0x04      N/A     skillNamePtr       char*       Pointer to skill name string\n  0x08+     N/A     skillData          struct      Remaining skill configuration data\n  Total: 0x1c bytes per element",
