      "signature": "void ClearAndDestroyTaskQueue(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Clears and destroys the concurrent task queue object at 0x0435b7b8.\n\nThis function is responsible for cleanup of a concurrent queue used for task\nscheduling. It drains all remaining items from the queue and then destroys the\nqueue object itself.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Setup exception handling frame (SEH) for cleanup guarantee\n2. Initialize vftable for concurrent_queue object at 0x0435b7b8\n3. Check if queue is empty using _Internal_empty()\n4. While queue is not empty:\n   - Dequeue one item using FUN_042f15f0() with parameter 0\n   - Check dequeue result (non-zero = success)\n   - Loop back to empty check\n5. Call _Internal_finish_clear() to complete the clearing operation\n6. Destroy the queue object using destructor ~_Concurrent_queue_base_v4()\n7. Restore exception handler and return\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses SEH (Structured Exception Handling) with FS:[0] register to ensure\n  destructor runs even if exception occurs during dequeue loop\n- The vftable initialization at 0x0432654e sets up virtual method dispatch\n  for concurrent queue operations\n- Global data at 0x0435b7b8 holds the queue state across function calls\n- XOR register at 0x04353080 is security cookie used to validate stack frame",
